parts":[{"text":"சிறிய","lemma":"ciṟiya","gloss":"small things"}],"gloss":"small things"},{"surface":"உணரா","parts":[{"text":"உணரா","lemma":"uṇarā","gloss":"not understanding"}],"gloss":"not understanding"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பீடு","parts":[{"text":"பீடு","lemma":"pīṭu","gloss":"greatness"}],"gloss":"greatness"},{"surface":"இன்று","parts":[{"text":"இன்று","lemma":"iṉṟu","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without"},{"surface":"பெருகிய","parts":[{"text":"பெருகிய","lemma":"perukiya","gloss":"increased"}],"gloss":"increased"},{"surface":"திருவின்","parts":[{"text":"திரு","lemma":"tiru","gloss":"wealth"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"-iṉ","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of wealth"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாடு","parts":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"pāṭu","gloss":"glory"}],"gloss":"glory"},{"surface":"இல்","parts":[{"text":"இல்","lemma":"il","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without"},{"surface":"மன்னரை","parts":[{"text":"மன்னர்","lemma":"maṉṉar","gloss":"kings"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"-ai","gloss":"accusative"}],"gloss":"kings"},{"surface":"பாடன்மார்","parts":[{"text":"பாடன்மார்","lemma":"pāṭaṉmār","gloss":"will not sing"}],"gloss":"will not sing"},{"surface":"எமரே","parts":[{"text":"எமர்","lemma":"emar","gloss":"our people"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"-ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"our people"}]}],"literal":"Shaking rays to bear, muddy pool / stability failing, ruined, leaning state, many legs / common place, one side, as a bed / drum-like trunk palmyra tree's saw-toothed big leaf-stalk / fiber and strip, with the drum, tying / by the plow living people's houses / in turn begging and eating, suffering life / patronage accepting noble people, who are they, saying / elephant-rope hanging, unceasing prosperity / mountain-adorned garden-land good country's lord / unfailing giving, anklet-wearing Āy / because there is no one else, to beat the drum, leaping / great rain-cloud over the sea having spread like, I too / thinking of you alone, came, therefore / poets' refuge having become, of the earth's bounds / may you endure, you alone / without you, empty having become, in this world / will they exist, patrons? approaching / even if praised greatly, even small things not understanding / greatness-less, increased wealth's / glory-less kings, will not sing, my people.","translation":"With a muddy pool that bears the shaking rays of the sun, using as a bed one side of the common assembly hall which has many leaning pillars, ruined and losing stability, tying our drum with the fiber and strips of the saw-toothed big leaf-stalks of the palmyra tree with a trunk like a drum, we live a suffering life, begging in turn for food at the houses of those who live by the plow. Asking, 'Who are the noble ones who will accept and patronize us?' O lord of the good country with mountain-adorned gardens, where elephant-ropes hang and prosperity never ceases! O Āy, wearing warrior anklets, whose giving never fails! Because there is no one else, to beat the drum and leap, just like a great rain-cloud that spreads over the sea, I too came thinking only of you. Therefore, having become the refuge of poets, may you alone endure as long as the bounds of the earth! In a world that has become empty without you, will there be any patrons? Even if praised greatly, they do not understand even small things; our people will never sing of those glory-less kings who possess great wealth but lack any greatness.","modern":"சூரியனின் அசையும் கதிர்களைத் தாங்கும் கலங்கலான குளத்தின் அருகே, நிலைதளர்ந்து சாய்ந்து விழும் பல தூண்களைக் கொண்ட பொதுச்சாவடியின் ஒரு பக்கத்தைப் படுக்கையாகக் கொண்டு, முரசு போன்ற அடிமரத்தைக் கொண்ட பனைமரத்தின் வாள் போன்ற பெரிய மடலின் நாரையும் வாரையும் கொண்டு எமது கிணைப்பறையைக் கட்டி, ஏர்த்தொழில் செய்து வாழ்பவர்களின் வீடுகளில் முறைமுறையாக இரந்து உண்ணும் துன்ப வாழ்க்கையை உடைய எமக்கு, 'ஆதரித்து வாரி வழங்கும் சான்றோர் யார்?' என்று வினவி, யானை கட்டும் கயிறுகள் தொங்கும், வளம் நீங்காத, மலைகள் சூழ்ந்த சோலைகளைக் கொண்ட நல்ல நாட்டின் தலைவனே! பொய்க்காத கொடையையும் வீரக்கழலையும் உடைய ஆய் மன்னனே! வறுமையால் எவரும் இல்லாத நிலையில், பறையடித்துப் பாடுவதற்கு, கடல் பரப்பில் பரந்து பெய்யும் பெருமழையைப் போல யானும் உன்னையே நினைத்து வந்தேன். ஆதலால், புலவர்களின் புகலிடமாக விளங்கும் நீ ஒருவன் மட்டுமே இந்நிலவுலகின் எல்லை உள்ளவரை நிலைபெற்று வாழ்வாயாக! நீ இல்லாததால் வறுமையுற்ற இவ்வுலகில், இரவலர்கள் அணுகிப் பாடுவதற்கு வேறு வள்ளல்கள் உளரோ? எவ்வளவு பெரிதாகப் புகழ்ந்து பாடினாலும் சிறிய அறிவும் இல்லாத, பெருமையற்ற, செல்வத்தை மட்டுமே பெருக்கிய, புகழில்லாத பிற மன்னர்களை எமது சுற்றத்தாராகிய பாணர்கள் பாடவே மாட்டார்கள்.","explanation":"The poet Uṟaiyūr ēṇiccēri Muṭamōciyār sings in praise of the chieftain Āy Aṇṭiraṉ in this Pāṭāṇ tiṇai poem. The poet describes the extreme poverty of the wandering bards who sleep in ruined public halls and tie their drums with cheap palmyra fibers, begging for food from poor farmers. Seeking a true patron, the poet compares his arrival to a massive rain-cloud that spreads over the ocean, seeking the generous Āy whose mountain country is rich and fertile. The poet blesses Āy to live forever as the sole refuge of scholars and poets. He concludes by stating that if Āy is gone, the world will be empty of true patrons, as other wealthy kings are ignorant and unworthy of being sung by noble poets.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.2],[1.2,1.6],[1.6,2.01],[2.15,3.1],[3.1,3.5],[3.5,4.16],[4.16,4.5],[4.5,5.5],[5.5,5.8],[5.8,6.3],[6.3,6.6],[7.22,7.53],[7.53,8.45],[8.45,8.76],[8.76,9.2],[9.2,9.53],[9.53,9.86],[9.86,10.3],[10.3,10.8],[10.8,11.23],[11.23,11.8],[11.8,12.3],[12.3,12.8],[12.8,13.8],[13.8,14.1],[14.1,14.5],[14.5,14.7],[14.7,15.1],[15.1,16.2],[16.2,16.8],[16.8,17.4],[17.4,17.64],[17.72,18.38],[18.38,18.82],[18.82,19.26],[19.26,19.96],[19.96,20.46],[20.46,20.76],[20.76,21.16],[21.16,21.76],[21.76,22.16],[22.36,22.91],[22.91,23.46],[23.46,24.36],[24.36,24.92],[24.92,25.66],[25.66,25.86],[25.86,26.64],[26.64,26.86],[26.86,27.61],[27.61,27.76],[27.76,28.36],[28.56,29.16],[29.16,29.76],[29.76,30.21],[30.21,30.96],[30.96,31.36],[31.36,3